---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Toddler Program - Marietta Childcare"
  description="Explore Marietta Childcare's Toddler Program for ages 12-36 months with language development, social skills, and play-based learning.">
  <section class="relative py-32 overflow-hidden w-screen -ml-[calc((100vw-100%)/2)]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
      <img 
        src="/images/Background_Images/child_watering_plant_garden_background.jpg" 
        alt="Toddler learning" 
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black mb-6 text-white drop-shadow-lg">Toddler Program</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mb-12 max-w-2xl text-white drop-shadow-md">Language development, social skills, and play-based learning for ages 12-36 months in an engaging environment.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 px-6 lg:px-20">
    <div class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-3xl mb-12">
        <p>
          Marietta Childcare's Toddler Program serves children ages 12 to 36 months with a focus on language development, social skills, and play-based learning. The Toddler Program at Marietta Childcare creates an engaging environment where toddlers explore, learn, and develop independence.
        </p>

        <h2>Language Development</h2>
        <p>
          Marietta Childcare's educators support language development through conversation, storytelling, songs, and interactive activities. The Toddler Program encourages communication skills and vocabulary expansion through responsive interactions and language-rich environments.
        </p>

        <h2>Social Skills Development</h2>
        <p>
          The Toddler Program at Marietta Childcare helps children develop social skills including sharing, turn-taking, and cooperative play. Marietta Childcare's educators model positive interactions and guide toddlers through social situations with patience and support.
        </p>

        <h2>Play-Based Learning</h2>
        <p>
          Marietta Childcare believes in the power of play for learning and development. The Toddler Program includes sensory activities, music, movement, art, and outdoor play that support cognitive, physical, and emotional growth.
        </p>

        <h2>Independence & Self-Care</h2>
        <p>
          Marietta Childcare supports toddlers in developing independence and self-care skills. The Toddler Program includes opportunities for toilet training readiness, self-feeding, and participation in daily routines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
        <div class="bg-primary/5 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-4">Program Features</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>✓ Language-rich environment</li>
            <li>✓ Social skills activities</li>
            <li>✓ Play-based curriculum</li>
            <li>✓ Music and movement</li>
            <li>✓ Art and creativity</li>
            <li>✓ Outdoor exploration</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-secondary/5 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-4">Age Range & Schedule</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>✓ Ages 12-36 months</li>
            <li>✓ Full-time enrollment</li>
            <li>✓ Part-time options</li>
            <li>✓ Flexible scheduling</li>
            <li>✓ Extended hours</li>
            <li>✓ School break care</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-primary/10 to-secondary/10 p-8 rounded-lg mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Toddler Development at Marietta Childcare</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">Marietta Childcare's Toddler Program supports the rapid development that occurs during ages 12-36 months. The Toddler Program creates a safe, stimulating environment where toddlers develop language, social skills, and independence.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-primary text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-full font-bold hover:scale-105 transition-transform">
          Schedule a Tour
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related Programs & Resources</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <a href="/programs/infant-care" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline">Infant Care Program →</a>
          <a href="/programs/preschool" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline">Preschool Program →</a>
          <a href="/resources/child-development" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline">Child Development Guide →</a>
          <a href="/resources/parenting-tips" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline">Parenting Tips →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
